# SRG-APP-000456-AU-000270  -  CAT I
# The Central Log Server must install security-relevant software updates
# within 30 days unless the time period is directed by an authoritative
# source (e.g., IAVM, CTOs, DTMs, STIGs).
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000456-AU-000270
group:           V-278988
severity:        high
cat:             CAT I
determination:   ORGANIZATIONAL
grade:           C
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-002605
control_rev5:    SI-2

contribution:    Nothing toward installation: the application can report its installed
                 version and build, but it has no setting that acquires, schedules or
                 applies a security-relevant update, so the 30-day installation objective
                 cannot be reached by configuring Splunk.

external:        The organization's flaw remediation procedure for Splunk Enterprise,
                 naming the authoritative source monitored (IAVM, CTO, DTM, STIG) and the
                 period within which security-relevant updates are installed.
external:        The configuration management record of upgrades performed, which is the
                 evidence of the installation period actually met.
external:        The vendor's currently supported release list, against which the installed
                 version and build are compared — the basis the attached product rule
                 SPLK-CL-000510 directs.
external:        The package or container image build and deployment pipeline that delivers
                 the replacement installation, assessed against its own baseline.

manual_reason:   Splunk Enterprise does not install its own software updates. An upgrade
                 replaces the installation from a vendor-supplied package, which is an
                 administrative act outside the product's configuration surface, and no key
                 in the specification set acquires, schedules or applies an update to the
                 instance; checks.tsv accordingly attaches no conf, stanza or key to this
                 requirement. The only update-related keys the product exposes are
                 notification or out of scope: web.conf.spec:192 updateCheckerBaseURL
                 merely causes Splunk Web to contact the vendor for notice of new versions
                 and can be set to 0 to stop that contact, app.conf.spec:116
                 show_upgrade_notification is app scope, and serverclass.conf.spec:316
                 updaterRunningFilter concerns deployment clients running a separately
                 installed self-updater rather than the Central Log Server itself. The
                 attached product rule SPLK-CL-000510 names no setting either — its fix
                 text directs an upgrade to a vendor-supported version and its check text
                 states that the STIG is sunset — so the determination rests on the
                 installed version and build, read from the running application but a
                 property of the installed software rather than a configurable value,
                 compared against the vendor's supported release list and against the flaw
                 remediation record.

citation:        SRG-APP-000456-AU-000270 check and fix text (CCI-002605, SI-2 c), severity
                 high; attached product rule SPLK-CL-000510, whose fix text directs an
                 upgrade to a vendor-supported version and whose check text states the STIG
                 is sunset — no configuration setting is named. No conf, stanza or key is
                 attached to this requirement in the mechanism inventory. Splunk 10.x
                 specification set (Version 10.0.0), keys enumerated and excluded as
                 non-installing: web.conf.spec:192 updateCheckerBaseURL (vendor
                 notification only, settable to 0); app.conf.spec:116
                 show_upgrade_notification (app scope); serverclass.conf.spec:316
                 updaterRunningFilter (deployment clients with a separately installed
                 self-updater).
finding:         Splunk Enterprise provides no setting that installs its own updates, so
                 this requirement is not decided by application configuration: a finding is
                 raised only where the installed version and build are no longer on the
                 vendor's supported release list, or where the flaw remediation record does
                 not show security-relevant updates installed within 30 days or within the
                 period an authoritative source directs, and it is recorded against the
                 organization's flaw remediation process and the installed software rather
                 than against the Splunk application configuration assessed here.
